#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:69
msgid "3. Change the Colour from the Phone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:71
msgid "Open LightBlue, tap **Scan** and connect to **SunFounder-C2**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:73
msgid "Expand the service **0xA002** and open the characteristic **C304**. Then tap **Write new value**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:78
msgid "Set the format in the top right corner to **UTF-8 String** and type ``R255G128B0``. The picture shows the field just before sending:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:83
msgid "Send it. The LED turns orange and the Serial Monitor prints ``colour: R255G128B0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:87
msgid "The sketch does not react to every single character. A BLE write can be split into several pieces on its way, so the sketch waits until the message is complete - a ``#`` at the end, or **120 ms** of silence - and only then sets the colour. If it acted on each piece, the LED would flash through the wrong colours on every send."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:92
msgid "Try a few more - the field stays open, so you can send again right away:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:98
msgid "Send this"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:99
msgid "What happens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:100
msgid "``R255G0B0``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:101
msgid "red"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:102
msgid "``R0G255B0``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:103
msgid "green"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:104
msgid "``R0G0B255``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:105
msgid "blue"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:106
msgid "``R255G255B255``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:107
msgid "white, all three channels at full"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:108
msgid "``R0G0B0``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:109
msgid "off"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:113
msgid "The numbers are **0 to 255**, not percentages. ``R128G0B0`` is a darker red than ``R255G0B0``, because the pin is switched on for only half of the time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:116
msgid "The whole message has to stay under **12 characters**, which is why there are no separators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:121
msgid "4. Code explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:123
msgid "**Three pins, one colour**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:131
msgid "``analogWrite(pin, 0..255)`` uses PWM, so the LED can show many colours - not just the three primary ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:134
msgid "**Splitting the message**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:144
msgid "The letter **R**, **G** or **B** marks where a number starts. Every character after a marker is added to that colour until the next marker arrives. That is why the order ``R...G...B...`` matters and why no brackets are needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:148
msgid "**From text to number**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:156
msgid "``toInt()`` converts the text ``\"255\"`` into the number 255. Forgetting it is a classic mistake - ``analogWrite`` would then act on garbage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:159
msgid "**The 12 character limit**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/iot_project_espc201/bluetooth_espc201/12-iot_Bluetooth_RGB_controller.rst:165
msgid "One BLE write carries at most 20 bytes and this sketch keeps a little headroom. ``R255G255B255`` is 12 characters - the longest useful message."
msgstr ""
